s></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRATA FUMIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOUDA CHIKAKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MORI YOICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAWA TSUTOMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WAKE RYOUSUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAZAKI MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUDA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRATA, FUMIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOUDA, CHIKAKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORI, YOICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAWA, TSUTOMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WAKE, RYOUSUKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAZAKI, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A coating composition capable of forming an alkali-soluble lubricating film excellent in suitability for press forming and dragging resistance, which comprises as major ingredients (A) a water-based polyurethane composition and (B) a lubricity-imparting agent contained in an amount of 1 to 30 wt.% based on the water-based polyurethane composition on a solid basis; and a metallic product which has been treated so as to have a lubricative surface and be excellent in press formability and dragging resistance, characterized by having been coated with the coating composition in a thickness of 0.5 to 5  mu m on a dry basis. Preferably, the coating composition contains as another major ingredient (C) silica particles in an amount of 1 to 30 wt.% based on the water-based polyurethane composition on a solid basis.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition de revêtement apte à former un film lubrifiant soluble dans les alcalis, particulièrement bien adapté au moulage par pressage et présentant une excellente résistance au frottement. Cette composition comprend comme principaux constituants (A) une composition polyuréthane à base d'eau et (B) entre 1 et 30 % en poids par rapport à la composition polyuréthane à base d'eau sur une base solide, d'un agent conférant un pouvoir lubrifiant; et un produit métallique traité de manière à comporter une surface lubrifiante et à se prêter particulièrement bien au moulage et à présenter une excellente résistance au frottement, se caractérisant par un revêtement d'une épaisseur de 0,5 à 5  mu m avec la composition de revêtement. Cette composition de revêtement contient de préférence comme autre principal constituant (C) entre 1 et 30 % en poids de particules de silice par rapport à la composition polyuréthane à base d'eau sur une base solide.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the